From b5b33cb0d0a3864fb8b5e285b4572637d950dec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Bain <ibain@mac.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:40:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Rivian: let MADS steering stay on when braking

Rivian was a MADS limited brand, so every brake press ended steering
no matter the setting. Drop it from that list so Remain Active/Pause
apply, and give it real off switches since there is no MADS button:
stalk up past the detent, shifting to P or R, or a fresh stalk-up
press once speed control is already off. One stalk-up while fully
engaged still only cancels speed control.
